          "id": "ef70dea7c85e5637f37828d75e5b9bb29dbfe513",
          "message": "Fix Reading beyond buffer end (#2384)\n\n* Validate signature lengths when verifying a signature.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Fix test build problem.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Fix test build problem.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Test invalid signature length.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Fix formating.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Update sig_stfl_xmss.h\n\nUpdate per review. Remove duplicate macro definition.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Updates per comments.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Fix formatting.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Update xmss tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Address test  failures.\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\n\n* Fix test_sig_stfl pthread path: activate and wire up rc2\n\nThe pthread branch in test_sig_stfl.c was gated on\nOQS_USE_PTHREADS_IN_TESTS, which stopped being defined when PR #1576\n(Oct 2023) migrated test_kem.c and test_sig.c to CMAKE_USE_PTHREADS_INIT.\ntest_sig_stfl.c (added later in PR #1650) kept using the old name, so\nits pthread branch has never compiled. Rename to OQS_USE_PTHREADS to\nmatch the sibling tests and activate the code.\n\nActivating the branch exposes two latent bugs introduced by the\ninvalid-signature test:\n- test_correctness_wrapper referenced `alg_name` (a main()-local) instead\n  of `td->alg_name`; fix to use the struct field.\n- thread_data_t.rc2 was set by the wrapper but never propagated back\n  into main()'s rc2 check, making the new invalid-signature test a\n  no-op on pthread builds. Initialize .rc2 = OQS_SUCCESS, copy td.rc2\n  after pthread_join, and include rc2 in the pthread-path exit check\n  to mirror the non-pthread path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\n\n* Fix test_sig_stfl rc_create flip for XMSS with key_sig_gen disabled\n\nIn the pthread path, test_create_keys runs sig_stfl_test_secret_key_lock,\nwhich for XMSS loads the keypair from a KAT file rather than calling\nkeygen. Its success does not depend on OQS_ALLOW_XMSS_KEY_AND_SIG_GEN,\nso unconditionally passing rc_create through update_test_result flipped\na legitimate SUCCESS into ERROR when key/sig gen was disabled, failing\nthe address-sanitizer-no-stfl-key-sig-gen CI job on\nXMSSMT-SHAKE_60/3_256.\n\nThis path was dead code until 53ad5be8 activated the pthread branch,\nwhich is why the bug surfaces now. LMS still falls through to real\nkeygen, so keep the flip for the non-XMSS case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\n\n* Skip pthread mutex stfl tests when key/sig gen is disabled\n\nCommit 53ad5be8 activated the pthread branch in test_sig_stfl.c,\nwhich runs three sequential threads (test_create_keys → test_sig_gen\n→ test_query_key) to exercise the lock/unlock paths around sign\noperations. That branch had been dead code before.\n\nWhen OQS_HAZARDOUS_EXPERIMENTAL_ENABLE_SIG_STFL_KEY_SIG_GEN is OFF,\nthese tests cannot meaningfully exercise what they are there to\ntest: there is no real sign pipeline to lock around. Whether setup\nsucceeds or fails then depends on whether the specific XMSS variant\nhas a KAT mapping in sig_stfl_KATs_keygen (some load from KAT and\nsucceed, others fall through to a disabled keygen and fail), which\nthe unconditional update_test_result flip cannot model for both\ncases at once — XMSSMT-SHAKE_60/3_256 (KAT-loaded) and\nXMSSMT-SHAKE_40/4_256 (keygen) fail in opposite directions.\n\nGate the three pthread tests on OQS_ALLOW_*_KEY_AND_SIG_GEN so they\nonly run in configs where sign is actually available. The existing\ntest_correctness_wrapper and test_secret_key_wrapper threads still\nrun and validate the expected-failure behavior via update_test_result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\n\n* Fix scan-build null-pointer warning in test_sig_stfl mutex init\n\nscan-build flagged pthread_mutex_init calls at line 1232 as potentially\nreceiving NULL, because it conservatively invalidates its knowledge of\nthe test_sk_lock/sk_lock globals across the intervening OQS_MEM_malloc\ncall. Use local pointers for the malloc results and assign to the\nglobals only after both mutexes are initialized. Also split the two\npthread_mutex_init calls so that a successfully-initialized first\nmutex is destroyed if the second init fails.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Norman Ashley <nashley@cisco.com>\nSigned-off-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\nCo-authored-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@uwaterloo.ca>\nCo-authored-by: Douglas Stebila <dstebila@users.noreply.github.com>",
